# Docker build-context excludes for the Vercel-less app image (Dockerfile / docker-compose.yml).
#
# Two reasons this file is load-bearing, not cosmetic:
#  1. CORRECTNESS — the Dockerfile runs `npm ci` (musl/alpine node_modules) and THEN `COPY . .`.
#     Without excluding node_modules, the host's glibc-built native modules (esbuild, zstd, …)
#     would overlay the freshly-installed musl ones and break the runtime image. node_modules
#     MUST be built inside the image, never copied in.
#  2. HYGIENE / SECURITY — this is an open-source repo built on developer machines. Never let a
#     local secret (.env*, tokens), VCS history (.git), or editor/agent state leak into an image
#     layer that might be pushed to a registry.

# Dependencies — always installed inside the image (see reason 1 above).
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Version control + agent/editor state.
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Vercel binding + build output (the image runs its OWN `eve build`).
.vercel
.output
**/.output
.nitro

# Workspace package build output — the image runs its OWN `build:packages`. Exclude the tsc
# incremental state WITH `dist`: a host `.tsbuildinfo` copied in without its `dist` makes tsc treat
# the package as up to date, skip the emit, and the image then has no package `dist`.
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local secrets / env — MUST NEVER be baked into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Runtime data (created at run time, mounted as volumes in docker-compose.yml).
.workflow-data
.open-everywhere-memory
.eve

# Logs, caches, OS cruft.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
coverage
.turbo
